      <h2 id="article-heading">Base64 Encoding Method, RFC 4648 &amp; Worked Vectors</h2>
      <p style="color: var(--text-muted); line-height: 1.7;">Base64 maps binary data into an ASCII subset of 64 characters: uppercase letters (A–Z), lowercase letters (a–z), digits (0–9), and two symbols (+ and /). Three 8-bit bytes (24 bits) are divided into four 6-bit values, increasing total payload length by exactly 33%.</p>

